WEBVTT

00:01.067 --> 00:04.093
- Most would agree.
- I don't agree.

00:04.170 --> 00:06.866
- Will you look at your skin?
- I am. What's the matter with it?

00:06.940 --> 00:08.874
- It's all blotchy.
- How? I don't see it.

00:08.942 --> 00:11.775
Dad, will you look at Sweet Dee's skin
and tell me it's not blotchy?

00:11.845 --> 00:13.938
- Do I have to listen to this shit all morning?
- Come on.

00:14.014 --> 00:15.743
Frank, you've gotta be kidding
with these receipts.

00:15.815 --> 00:17.783
We were actually doing better
before you took over.

00:17.851 --> 00:21.719
Hey! Hey! What's up, guys?
I didn't hear you guys come in.

00:21.788 --> 00:24.518
Uh, you know, I was actually in here
early opening up this morning...

00:24.591 --> 00:26.525
Charlie, we had an agreement.

00:26.593 --> 00:28.686
This is a place of business,
not your home.

00:28.762 --> 00:32.289
- Uh, yeah, I know that.
- Not supposed to sleep in the bar anymore, bro.

00:32.365 --> 00:34.697
- I wasn't.
- You didn't come home last night.

00:34.768 --> 00:37.236
Oh, okay, okay.
Well, guess what.

00:37.303 --> 00:41.069
- I found some extensive water damage in the back office.
- What?

00:41.141 --> 00:43.109
Yeah, so, maybe
I'm not such a bad guy...

00:43.176 --> 00:45.406
for passing out in there
and drinking too much or whatever.

00:45.478 --> 00:49.778
- That's a terrible excuse, dude.
- Well, I drank too much, so lay off.

00:49.849 --> 00:52.374
Holy shit! Guys, come here!
Come here! Check this out!

00:52.452 --> 00:54.443
Look!

00:54.521 --> 00:56.648
- What?
- What?

00:56.723 --> 00:58.953
That is the Virgin Mary.

00:59.025 --> 01:01.653
- What?
- Oh, take it easy, bro.

01:01.728 --> 01:03.787
No, look. The head
and the arms and the cape.

01:03.863 --> 01:05.558
- Does look like it. Weird.
- I don't see it.

01:05.632 --> 01:08.567
What if it's a sign?
You guys, remember, I wanted to be a priest.

01:08.635 --> 01:13.265
- That's a water stain, dude.
- Or it could be a sign that we need to get our pipes fixed.

01:13.339 --> 01:16.103
What if it's a miracle?

01:16.176 --> 01:20.545
Listen. It could be a miracle.
It could be bullshit.

01:20.613 --> 01:22.945
There's only one thing
we know for sure.

01:23.016 --> 01:26.747
- What's that?
- It's a goddamn gold mine.

02:01.287 --> 02:03.517
Well, I'll tell you, Jim.
I was in the back office...

02:03.590 --> 02:06.525
and I'd just finished praying
on my rosaries.

02:06.593 --> 02:09.653
And I was doing some crunches,
you know, working on my abs.

02:09.729 --> 02:11.959
And that's when I saw it.

02:12.031 --> 02:14.124
And I thought to myself...

02:14.200 --> 02:16.327
"That is definitely
the mother of our Lord."

02:16.402 --> 02:19.269
Did my face look fat?

02:19.339 --> 02:22.206
- Yeah.
- No, don't-don't screw with me here.

02:22.275 --> 02:24.675
- Seriously. It's just the TV, right?
- No, it's been looking fat.

02:24.744 --> 02:30.341
So, if you like the Virgin Mary and you like beer,
come on down to Paddy's Pub.

02:30.416 --> 02:35.319
- We got 'em both.
- Welcome to Paddy's Pub, home of the Blessed Mother.

02:35.388 --> 02:38.846
- Would you care to make a donation?
- How much should I give?

02:38.925 --> 02:43.453
Well, what price can one put on
the viewing of a miracle?

02:43.530 --> 02:46.431
Give whatever you can.

02:49.002 --> 02:51.061
These people are pathetic.

02:51.137 --> 02:54.038
Yeah, Dad, I really don't feel very good
about what we're doing in here.

02:54.107 --> 02:56.041
Well, don't get all
high-and-mighty on me.

02:56.109 --> 02:59.545
I only made four dollars, Deandra.
I think I can live with myself.

02:59.612 --> 03:03.776
Let's move, lady. We got a long line here.
Don't be selfish. All right. Rollin' on in.

03:03.850 --> 03:06.478
This is one of the more ridiculous things
we have ever done, dude.

03:06.553 --> 03:09.545
I will tell you what is ridiculous...
Taking advantage of the mother of God.

03:09.622 --> 03:12.420
Are you kidding me?
That is a water stain, man.

03:12.492 --> 03:15.325
We are really pushing our luck
with the big guy upstairs on this one.

03:15.395 --> 03:19.229
Dude, if you don't think you're going to hell,
you need to take a long look at yourself.

03:19.299 --> 03:21.392
- Go look at yourself, bro.
- Okay, I'll do that.

03:21.467 --> 03:24.129
- Yeah, do it.
- Dee Reynolds?

03:24.204 --> 03:27.901
Oh, wow. It is you.
Matthew Mara.

03:27.974 --> 03:31.740
We were in physical therapy together
twice a week after school.

03:31.811 --> 03:34.780
I was the only other person
in physical therapy with you.

03:34.847 --> 03:38.044
- Huh.
- I wore the giant leg braces.

03:38.117 --> 03:41.143
- Oh, my God. Yeah, with the leg braces.
- Yeah.

03:41.221 --> 03:45.282
- Wow. You look different.
- Yeah, so do you. No more back brace, I see.

03:45.358 --> 03:47.724
- You look wonderful. Yeah.
- Oh.

03:47.794 --> 03:49.989
- Matty Mara?
- Hello, Mac.

03:50.063 --> 03:53.089
I knew it! I called it from across the bar,
even without the cripple braces.

03:53.166 --> 03:57.296
- So, what? You're a priest now?
- Wow! Look at you. Little Matty Mara all grown up, huh?

03:57.370 --> 04:00.999
- Hey, Dennis, little Matty Mara's here.
- Hey-oh!

04:01.074 --> 04:03.065
Hey, you come to witness
the miracle for yourself?

04:03.142 --> 04:06.771
Miracle's a strong word, Mac.
We don't just throw that around like a football.

04:06.846 --> 04:10.407
- Well, you should.
- Well, I just came out of curiosity.

04:10.483 --> 04:13.475
See what you had
at this bar of yours.

04:13.553 --> 04:16.386
- You have to admit it's her, dude.
- Well, it's quite a likeness.

04:16.456 --> 04:19.050
- Yeah. You think it's a sign?
- No, it's a stain.

04:19.125 --> 04:21.855
But, uh, it's an interesting stain.
I'll give you that.

04:21.928 --> 04:24.192
- Hey, Matty.
- Hello, Dennis. How are you?

04:24.264 --> 04:26.198
I've been better.
I've been better.

04:26.266 --> 04:29.793
Let me ask you a question, man. I know
it's been years since we've seen each other...

04:29.869 --> 04:31.928
but does my face look fat to you?

04:32.005 --> 04:35.304
Well, we've all put on a few pounds
since high school, so...

04:35.375 --> 04:37.639
Of course. Of course.
But I don't look fat though, right?

04:37.710 --> 04:40.008
Um, no.

04:40.079 --> 04:42.377
- What did we call you in high school?
- Rickety Cricket, dude!

04:42.448 --> 04:45.713
That's right. Rickety Crickety Legs.

04:45.785 --> 04:47.980
Yeah, his legs were...

04:48.054 --> 04:51.854
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Hey, remember how you would pass out at parties...

04:51.924 --> 04:54.688
- and Dennis would tea-bag you?
- Yeah, then I would take the photo.

04:54.761 --> 04:59.460
We'd pass it around the school.
Everybody loved those photos, Matty.

04:59.532 --> 05:02.194
- Hey, you still get balls-to-the-chin cracks?
- No.

05:02.268 --> 05:04.498
Actually, that was a long time ago.

05:04.570 --> 05:06.800
- It would be funnier as a priest.
- Oh, my God. Those...

05:06.873 --> 05:09.034
- Those were hilarious.
- You don't understand how much everybody loved those.

05:09.108 --> 05:11.906
- My balls on your chin.
- Everybody loved you, man.

05:11.978 --> 05:14.503
I think people still have copies.
There's a lot floating around.

05:14.580 --> 05:18.038
- I saw them on the Internet!
- You were, like, famous in school.

05:18.117 --> 05:21.382
- Yeah, practically. I got a whole shoe box of those things.
- That's partially our doing.

05:21.454 --> 05:25.049
- Well, let's... let's... I should get going, so, um...
- Okay.

05:25.124 --> 05:27.058
Hey, hey. Check it out though.

05:27.126 --> 05:31.324
Um, why did you pause
before you said "no" earlier?

05:31.397 --> 05:33.490
I'm sorry?

05:33.566 --> 05:36.865
Well, earlier when I asked you
if my face looked fat, you kind of paused.

05:36.936 --> 05:39.700
I'm not sure.

05:39.772 --> 05:42.434
Uh, listen, Dee, it was
great seeing you again.

05:42.508 --> 05:45.841
- Oh, yeah. You too.
- Gentlemen.

05:45.912 --> 05:48.380
- Cricket. - Later, Cricks.
- See you, Rickety Crickety.

05:48.448 --> 05:50.382
- I love that guy.
- How do you know the priest?

05:50.450 --> 05:53.283
- Went to high school with him.
- We should get him to bless the stain.

05:53.353 --> 05:55.548
- Why?
- This could be huge, Charlie.

05:55.621 --> 05:58.215
I mean, endorsement from
the Catholic Church.

05:58.291 --> 06:01.124
No. No. See, you guys are
taking this thing way too far.

06:01.194 --> 06:03.424
You know what I'm gonna do?
Wash my hands of it.

06:03.496 --> 06:05.760
Washing my hands of
the whole situation, Lord.

06:05.832 --> 06:08.460
He will smite you all.
God will smite you all!

06:08.534 --> 06:12.231
Okay, uh, we should do it soon though
because the pipe might leak a little more.

06:12.305 --> 06:15.297
The stain could fade.
You think this priest would help you guys?

06:15.375 --> 06:17.400
- I think Dee could get him to do it.
- Yeah.

06:17.477 --> 06:19.809
- What? Why me?
- Oh, "Why me?" she says.

06:19.879 --> 06:22.609
The guy was in love with her.
He would do anything for her.

06:22.682 --> 06:25.378
- No.
- All right. Remember the time you said you'd kiss him...

06:25.451 --> 06:27.385
- if he ate a horse turd?
- He ate the whole turd.

06:27.453 --> 06:30.354
The guy eats the whole thing.
Then she doesn't kiss him 'cause...

06:30.423 --> 06:32.721
His breath smelled like shit.

06:32.792 --> 06:35.727
- That's my girl.
- It didn't really happen like that.

06:35.795 --> 06:38.263
No. He ate the whole turd,
and then she wouldn't kiss him.

06:38.331 --> 06:41.789
- Hey, come on. This would be really good for the bar.
- No. Screw you guys. No way.

06:41.868 --> 06:46.134
- That's a bad attitude.
- The priest may not do it because she's getting old.

06:46.205 --> 06:48.469
- Oh! Yeah.
- What is that?

06:48.541 --> 06:50.907
- Your skin's all blotchy.
- No, it's not.

06:50.977 --> 06:53.639
- He's not gonna do it. You got the crow's-feet.
- Crow's-feet.

06:53.713 --> 06:56.079
- No, I don't.
- You're getting the lines there.

06:56.149 --> 06:58.083
Mmm. Five head. Laugh lines.

06:58.151 --> 07:00.915
You know what?
You guys are such assholes.

07:00.987 --> 07:03.148
I'm gonna see what I can do.

07:06.826 --> 07:09.192
Take care. Bye.

07:09.262 --> 07:11.492
Matthew, hi.

07:11.564 --> 07:14.863
Dee. Wow. What a nice surprise.
What brings you here?

07:14.934 --> 07:20.133
Well, the guys and I kind of needed somebody
to come and bless that stain in our bar.

07:22.375 --> 07:24.639
- Are you serious?
- Mm-hmm.

07:24.710 --> 07:27.110
Dee, I'm not gonna bless
a water stain.

07:27.180 --> 07:29.273
We don't do things like that.
The Catholic Church...

07:29.348 --> 07:31.282
Oh, no, no, no.
I know not them.

07:31.350 --> 07:33.318
I was hoping you could
do me a favor.

07:34.921 --> 07:38.220
I realize you were able to get me
to do things for you in school, but...

07:38.291 --> 07:43.422
Oh, you know what? I did. I kind of led you on
a little bit back then, didn't I?

07:43.496 --> 07:46.021
But I wasn't always a tease, you know?

07:46.098 --> 07:48.498
Remember? I let you do
all my math homework.

07:48.568 --> 07:51.366
Not sure I follow your logic.

07:51.437 --> 07:54.031
Well, what about that time
we almost kissed?

07:54.106 --> 07:56.734
You made me eat a...

07:56.809 --> 07:58.743
Look, I'm not blessing
the stain, okay?

07:58.811 --> 08:01.644
- Oh, no. Hold on a second.
- I mean, the taste of that thing alone...

08:01.714 --> 08:03.648
- No, I can't imagine.
- It haunts me.

08:03.716 --> 08:06.549
Of course it does.
I'm sorry, okay? Forget...

08:06.619 --> 08:09.247
Forget I came by about the stain.
I don't care about that anymore.

08:09.322 --> 08:13.884
I just... I know you really liked me back then,
and I know I wasn't very nice to you.

08:13.960 --> 08:17.487
And I think that's just because I was too stupid
to realize how wonderful you are.

08:17.563 --> 08:19.531
I'm sorry.

08:19.599 --> 08:24.036
And for the record, I think that
you grew up to be very handsome.

08:24.103 --> 08:27.698
You do realize you're leading me on right now?
I'm a priest.

08:27.773 --> 08:30.207
- Am I? Oh, I didn't even know.
- Yeah.

08:31.811 --> 08:34.041
But if you wanted to grab
a drink sometime...

08:34.113 --> 08:36.604
- You're still doing it.
- Oh, my God. I don't...

08:36.682 --> 08:39.708
Wow, I... I think it's just 'cause
you look so handsome in...

08:39.785 --> 08:41.514
- Please leave.
- Okay, I'm gonna go now.

08:41.587 --> 08:43.214
- Thank you. It would be best.
- All right.

08:43.289 --> 08:45.587
- God bless.
- Yeah.

08:48.294 --> 08:51.889
Would you care to make a donation in
the name of Paddy's Pub to the Blessed Mother?

08:51.964 --> 08:55.127
- Mm-mmm.
- Charlie, this needs to stop. If you guys don't do it...

08:55.201 --> 08:58.102
- I'm gonna do it myself.
- You're telling me. I'm sick of doing this.

08:58.170 --> 09:01.731
- God is going to show his wrath, Charlie.
- Excuse me.

09:01.807 --> 09:05.903
Are you the young man to whom
the Holy Mother first appear?

09:05.978 --> 09:08.538
- Yeah.
- Could you bless me, please?

09:08.614 --> 09:11.777
- You want me to bless you?
- Please, senor.

09:11.851 --> 09:15.719
Uh, yeah, sure, I guess.

09:15.788 --> 09:19.485
- In the name of the Father, the Son, Holy Spirit. Amen.
- Right hand.

09:19.559 --> 09:23.461
- Gracias.
- You're welcome.

09:23.529 --> 09:25.463
Did you see that, dude?

09:25.531 --> 09:27.465
I just blessed that woman.

09:27.533 --> 09:30.559
I may have saved that poor,
wretched old person's life.

09:30.636 --> 09:32.627
Well, I don't know
about that, but, uh...

09:32.705 --> 09:34.639
This could be my calling, Charlie.

09:34.707 --> 09:37.335
What happened to all that
God's wrath business, and this has to end...

09:37.410 --> 09:41.141
Yeah, I know. Don't worry about that, dude.
I think this could actually be a good thing.

09:41.213 --> 09:43.579
- We could change the world.
- Okay, okay. All right.

09:43.649 --> 09:47.107
New plan, all right?
Let's go around, let's bless people.

09:47.186 --> 09:50.417
Well, actually, I should bless people though,
but you could be my right-hand man.

09:50.489 --> 09:52.855
- You could be my Peter.
- Oh.

09:52.925 --> 09:54.859
Okay, I'll be your Peter.

09:54.927 --> 09:57.987
- Dress a little nicer though,
'cause you look like shit.

09:58.064 --> 10:00.897
Hey. How'd it go with the priest?

10:00.967 --> 10:03.902
- Not gonna happen.
- Did you put the moves on him?

10:03.970 --> 10:06.803
First of all, gross. I don't think
you're supposed to whore out your kids.

10:06.872 --> 10:09.067
Second of all, that guy
is a really good person...

10:09.141 --> 10:11.075
and I've treated him
like shit his whole life.

10:11.143 --> 10:14.112
- For once I'm gonna do the right thing.
- He thinks you're too old, huh?

10:14.180 --> 10:16.546
Goddamn it.
Why do I speak to you, ever?

10:16.616 --> 10:20.950
- Hello.
- Oh, wow.

10:21.020 --> 10:22.612
What is wrong with you?

10:22.688 --> 10:26.180
Oh, well, I've been fasting for three days,
so I probably look good.

10:26.258 --> 10:30.058
- You haven't eaten anything for three days?
- And I feel great.

10:30.129 --> 10:31.858
Why the hell are you fasting?

10:31.931 --> 10:35.833
I thought I would get in the spirit of
the religious aspect of what we got going.

10:35.901 --> 10:38.301
- It's 'cause we said his face looks fat.
- It is not.

10:38.371 --> 10:40.464
- People have been fasting for thousands of years...
- Face looks fat.

10:40.539 --> 10:43.975
- For health and religious purposes. Moses...
- Fat face.

10:44.043 --> 10:47.342
- Jesus and Moses in the woods and in the desert...
- Pretty fat, right? Fat.

10:47.413 --> 10:49.973
- Please listen to me. Please.
- Forget it.

10:50.049 --> 10:53.018
- Yeah.
- All right? The priest thinks Dee's too old for him.

10:53.085 --> 10:56.919
We gotta go to plan "B."
I know another guy who could help us.

11:01.227 --> 11:03.695
Father O'Grady? Uh...

11:03.763 --> 11:05.856
I'm Frank Reynolds.
I was in your parish.

11:05.931 --> 11:09.367
- What do you want?
- We came to talk to you about a stain.

11:09.435 --> 11:13.565
No! Uh, wait a second.
We just wanna have a few words with you.

11:13.639 --> 11:16.938
We found a stain in our bar
that resembles the Virgin Mary.

11:17.009 --> 11:19.876
- Cats are brown now.
- What?

11:19.945 --> 11:23.244
The cats are brown.

11:23.315 --> 11:25.408
What in the hell is
he talking about?

11:25.484 --> 11:28.942
This guy's perfect.
Let's go clean him up.

11:41.132 --> 11:43.464
What are you doing?

11:47.438 --> 11:50.271
- What is that?
- What? It's like...

11:50.341 --> 11:52.502
- Why are you dressed like this?
- Come on. It's perfect.

11:52.577 --> 11:55.341
- Where did you get it?
- I have my sources.

11:55.413 --> 11:57.881
I told you to dress nice.
We look like salt and pepper shakers.

11:57.949 --> 12:00.417
- Ah, we look good.
- All right. Let's just get started.

12:00.485 --> 12:02.783
- Um...
- Mmm.

12:02.854 --> 12:04.822
Ah. Uh, excuse me, sir.

12:04.889 --> 12:07.881
- Hello. Uh, would you like a blessing?
- From who?

12:07.959 --> 12:11.087
- Well, it was to me that the Virgin Mary first appeared.
- Well, I found it.

12:11.162 --> 12:13.596
- What?
- Well, I'm just saying I was the one who found it.

12:13.664 --> 12:16.929
Yes, but, uh, I was the one who first
recognized it was the Virgin Mary.

12:17.001 --> 12:19.834
- I found it, if you want the truth.
- You thought it was a stain.

12:19.904 --> 12:22.702
I'd much prefer a blessing from him.

12:22.774 --> 12:26.540
- Why?
- He seems a lot more religious than you.

12:26.611 --> 12:28.841
He is my number two
and doesn't really do the same...

12:28.913 --> 12:31.939
- Well, maybe I could just throw you one of...
- Don't do it.

12:32.016 --> 12:34.917
Don't do it, Charlie. Don't do it!

12:37.522 --> 12:39.922
- Ha!
- Thanks a lot. I appreciate it.

12:39.991 --> 12:43.188
Okay, feel better.
You're looking better already to me.

12:43.261 --> 12:47.527
- You are completely betraying me. You're supposed to be my Peter.
- You know what, dude?

12:47.598 --> 12:50.965
Hear me out for a second.
Now, technically, that stain did appear to me.

12:51.035 --> 12:54.129
Also, I am familiar with carpentry
and I don't know who my father is...

12:54.205 --> 12:56.139
so am I the messiah?

12:56.207 --> 12:58.368
I don't know. Could be.
I'm not ruling it out.

12:58.443 --> 13:00.877
- The messiah?
- I'm just not ruling it out, is all.

13:00.945 --> 13:04.039
- You gotta be kidding me, dude.
- Well, the Lord works in mysterious ways.

13:04.115 --> 13:06.208
I knew you were gonna ruin this.
Goddamn it.

13:06.284 --> 13:08.752
Ooh. I really wish you
wouldn't take my name in vain.

13:13.825 --> 13:18.228
How are we gonna get this guy
to bless anything? He's out ofhis mind.

13:19.597 --> 13:21.929
Well, I'm hoping it's
mostly the booze talking.

13:21.999 --> 13:24.263
Let's find some coffee.
We can sober him up.

13:26.170 --> 13:29.139
- Did you hear me?
- Hmm?

13:29.207 --> 13:31.675
Dennis, I think you
really gotta eat.

13:31.742 --> 13:34.404
No, I just spaced out
for a second. What's up?

13:34.479 --> 13:36.947
- Find some coffee. We don't have a ton of time.
- Yeah.

13:38.683 --> 13:41.948
Here's a confession.
I'm in love with a man.

13:43.020 --> 13:44.954
What?

13:45.022 --> 13:47.081
I'm in love with a man...

13:47.158 --> 13:49.991
a man called God.

13:50.061 --> 13:54.020
Does that make me gay?
Am I gay for God?

13:54.098 --> 13:56.726
- You betcha.
- Can I talk to you, please?

13:56.801 --> 13:58.792
- Speaketh.
- In private.

13:58.870 --> 14:01.964
Okay.

14:02.039 --> 14:04.303
Well, congratulations, Jim Jones.

14:04.375 --> 14:07.401
You found the four people on the planet
dumb enough to listen to your shit.

14:07.478 --> 14:09.708
Oh, forgive him, Lord,
for he know not what he say.

14:09.780 --> 14:12.715
Give it a rest. You're not the messiah.
You don't know dick about the Bible.

14:12.783 --> 14:15.308
You know, it really sounds like
somebody in this room is jealous.

14:15.386 --> 14:17.718
Because it's bullshit!
I'm the one that wanted to become a priest...

14:17.788 --> 14:20.814
I'm the one that knew it was Mary,
I'm the one that should have followers.

14:20.892 --> 14:23.486
- Sorry, bro. You suck at it.
- You wanna have a little competition?

14:23.561 --> 14:26.530
- Like what?
- Let's go toe-to-toe on the Bible, bitch.

14:26.597 --> 14:30.693
Ask and ye shall receive, sucker.

14:33.671 --> 14:39.507
Forgive me, Father, for I have sinned.
It has been 10 years since my last confession.

14:41.579 --> 14:45.640
In the name of the Father, the Son and
the Holy Spirit, what's on your mind, my dear?

14:45.716 --> 14:48.150
I'm in love with a man
that I can't have, Father.

14:48.219 --> 14:51.882
And he used to love me too,
but then I was really mean to him...

14:51.956 --> 14:54.220
and now we'll never know
what could have been.

14:54.292 --> 14:56.886
Well, it's too late now.

14:56.961 --> 14:59.521
He's made a commitment
that can never be broken.

14:59.597 --> 15:03.829
Let's drop this act, Matty.
Listen, I think I have really strong feelings for you.

15:03.901 --> 15:05.892
Dee, please don't do this.

15:05.970 --> 15:08.404
You know what? It just seems
like some kind of cruel joke.

15:08.472 --> 15:11.270
I mean, you wanted me once,
and now that you can have me...

15:11.342 --> 15:17.008
And, oh, Matty, I mean you could really,
really have me.

15:17.081 --> 15:19.072
You don't want it anymore?

15:19.150 --> 15:21.846
Well, God has a plan for everybody.

15:21.919 --> 15:24.444
- Well, that seems dumb.
- Well, it's not. It's God's plan.

15:24.522 --> 15:27.685
- Yeah, well, God's plan sucks this time. You know why?
- Mmm.

15:27.758 --> 15:29.988
- 'Cause I think I love you, Matthew.
- Don't say that, Dee.

15:30.061 --> 15:32.427
I have to say it,
and I'm gonna tell you why.

15:32.496 --> 15:36.159
Because if I don't say it,
I'm gonna regret it for the rest of my life.

15:36.233 --> 15:39.396
Okay, maybe that's not "God's plan"
or whatever. I don't care.

15:39.470 --> 15:41.597
I want you to know something.
I love you.

15:41.672 --> 15:46.939
And I... I could be your wife, and I could spend
the rest of my days making you happy.

15:47.011 --> 15:50.640
- Dee?
- Yes. It's me.

15:50.715 --> 15:53.878
- I know it's you. Just please, please leave.
- No, listen. Wait, wait, wait.

15:53.951 --> 15:56.249
I don't know what God
wants for us, all right?

15:56.320 --> 15:58.481
But I do know God
brought you into our bar...

15:58.556 --> 16:01.719
and maybe that was just so I could say I'm sorry,
but that sounds stupid.

16:01.792 --> 16:04.761
I don't think that's why. That's not big enough.
He works bigger than that.

16:04.829 --> 16:08.230
Maybe his plan is for us to be together
because he did have you come to our bar. Matty?

16:08.299 --> 16:10.631
- What?
- Open the door.

16:10.701 --> 16:12.635
- No.
- Matty, open the door.

16:12.703 --> 16:14.637
I love you.

16:14.705 --> 16:16.639
- I know that.
- Okay.

16:16.707 --> 16:19.198
- Say seven Hail Marys.
- Hold on. Hold on. Hold on.

16:19.276 --> 16:21.676
I love you.

16:23.881 --> 16:27.840
"When the Lord saw that he had
gone over to look at the burning bush...

16:27.918 --> 16:29.852
"God called from within.

16:29.920 --> 16:33.686
'Moses, come no closer!
Remove your sandals, for"'...

16:33.758 --> 16:38.092
Uh, let's stop there.
Why is God asking Moses to remove his sandals?

16:38.162 --> 16:42.758
Well, you didn't let me finish, dude.
It's because Moses is about to walk on holy ground.

16:42.833 --> 16:45.301
- No, actually, it's not.
- Yes, it is. That's the next line.

16:45.369 --> 16:50.068
"Remove your sandals, for the place
where you are standing is holy ground."

16:50.141 --> 16:52.132
But what's in between the lines?

16:52.209 --> 16:56.202
What's in between the lines is that
he has to take off his damn sandals...

16:56.280 --> 16:58.714
because it's sacred ground.

16:58.783 --> 17:01.251
No! Sacred ground?
Sacred ground?

17:01.318 --> 17:04.344
God doesn't worship the ground.
God made the ground.

17:04.422 --> 17:08.950
And Moses is about to step near a burning bush.
That is gonna be hot.

17:09.026 --> 17:11.085
God doesn't think Moses
is gonna do it.

17:11.162 --> 17:13.722
"Hey, Moses, kick your shoes off.

17:13.798 --> 17:16.665
Come on. Walk around
a burning bush"?

17:16.734 --> 17:21.034
You know, that's like asking me
to take my shoes off and stand on a hot plate.

17:21.105 --> 17:24.506
I'm not gonna do it...
unless God asks me to.

17:24.575 --> 17:26.634
And then I am, just like Moses.

17:26.711 --> 17:28.645
Why? What's gonna happen to Moses?

17:28.713 --> 17:30.840
His feet aren't gonna get burned.

17:30.915 --> 17:35.215
No. God is gonna reward him
with some sweet-ass shoes.

17:35.286 --> 17:39.313
It's like,
"Oh. Oh. You risk your feet, you get some shoes."

17:41.092 --> 17:44.118
That's the way God works,
'cause God loves us.

17:44.195 --> 17:47.858
Trust in God, he'll give you shoes.

17:47.932 --> 17:50.924
Are you kidding me?

17:51.001 --> 17:52.935
You're buying this crap? You...

17:53.003 --> 17:55.028
All right. Here we go.

17:55.172 --> 17:58.699
- Right foot, left foot, right foot, left foot.
- What are you doing? Who's this?

17:58.776 --> 18:00.710
This crazy, drunk priest...

18:00.778 --> 18:02.712
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
No, no, no, no, no.

18:02.780 --> 18:05.271
- You get a drink after you bless the stain.
- Shh!

18:05.349 --> 18:09.115
Ooh, cats!
And they're brown!

18:09.186 --> 18:11.780
Oh, this guy is great.
Hey, you think he'll bless me?

18:11.856 --> 18:14.347
- Love to.
- Great. Hey!

18:14.425 --> 18:16.655
It's okay, Frank.
Hey, everybody, gather round.

18:16.727 --> 18:20.163
This priest here
is going to bless me.

18:20.231 --> 18:25.635
Then after he's finished, I will honor each and
every one of you with a blessing of your own.

18:25.703 --> 18:28.831
You can take that with you.
Okay, Father. Anytime you're ready.

18:29.740 --> 18:34.473
The Father, Son and Holy Spirit.

18:34.545 --> 18:36.877
What is wrong with you, old man?

18:36.947 --> 18:39.313
- Why would you bring
somebody like this into the bar?

18:39.383 --> 18:42.079
Charlie, get the camcorder.
The father's gonna bless the stain.

18:42.153 --> 18:44.018
Right foot, left foot.
There we go.

18:44.088 --> 18:48.821
- Dee. Dee.
- Whoa. You are not lookin' good, huh?

18:48.893 --> 18:51.088
Truth, truth. Face fat?

18:51.162 --> 18:53.426
No, you idiot.
Your face is fine.

18:53.497 --> 18:55.488
I just got mad that
you called mine blotchy.

18:56.634 --> 18:58.966
- Oh. Why-Why-Why...
- What?

18:59.036 --> 19:02.904
- Why you do that?
- Oh, um, because you're a bad person.

19:02.973 --> 19:05.441
- Charlie, you got the camcorder?
- Oh, yeah, yeah, I got it.

19:05.509 --> 19:09.377
- Oh, Mac, Mac. This endorsement's gonna put me over the top.
- Go to hell, Charlie.

19:09.446 --> 19:12.006
Oh, these people are gonna
be eating out of my divine hands.

19:12.082 --> 19:16.109
- These people are gonna catch on to your shit.
- Are they really? Hello.

19:19.957 --> 19:22.949
No! No, get away from there!

19:23.027 --> 19:25.860
- Get him away!
- Get... Back off. Oh.

19:25.930 --> 19:28.421
- What did you do, you shithead? You ruined it!
- Yeah.

19:28.499 --> 19:30.592
Oh! It's gone!

19:30.668 --> 19:32.932
- Uh, no, actually, it's not gone.
- It's gone!

19:33.003 --> 19:36.097
- The Virgin Mary has left us!
- No, she hasn't left us!

19:36.173 --> 19:41.577
- You can see the outline.
- She abandoned us 'cause we listen to a false prophet!

19:41.645 --> 19:44.239
- No! False pro...
- False prophet.

19:44.315 --> 19:47.216
- That's what you are, a false prophet.
- Where are you going?

19:47.284 --> 19:49.548
- Looks like your followers are leaving you.
- No!

19:49.620 --> 19:52.054
Don't go. She'll come back.

19:52.122 --> 19:54.056
She'll come back.

19:54.124 --> 19:57.184
- Dee.
- Matthew? What are you doing here?

19:57.261 --> 20:00.389
I thought about what you said,
and I think you're right.

20:00.464 --> 20:04.560
I mean, in some weird way,
this was God's plan for us.

20:04.635 --> 20:07.399
I mean, I had to become a priest
to reconnect with you...

20:07.471 --> 20:11.999
- and I had to leave the priesthood to have you.
- Huh?

20:12.076 --> 20:14.601
Mr. Reynolds, I'd like to ask for
your daughter's hand in marriage.

20:14.678 --> 20:16.669
- Done.
- Okay, hold on one second.

20:16.747 --> 20:20.581
- Bless you.
- Hold on. Did you just say that you left the priesthood?

20:20.651 --> 20:22.812
Yes! Yes, I had to.

20:22.887 --> 20:26.152
- Matty, wow. You should not have done that.
- What do you mean?

20:26.223 --> 20:30.091
You gotta... You should go
and undo that right now.

20:30.160 --> 20:33.027
- Uh, but you said...
- Yeah, I know what I said.

20:33.097 --> 20:36.624
There were a lot of things,
and I meant all of them. I did.

20:36.700 --> 20:40.192
But the thing is, I didn't know you were
actually gonna leave the Church...

20:40.271 --> 20:45.106
which is why I felt safe saying
those things in the first place.

20:45.175 --> 20:48.804
So wait. Wait. So...

20:48.879 --> 20:50.870
S-So you don't love me?

20:50.948 --> 20:55.817
Oh, Matty.
I think you are a great guy.

20:55.886 --> 20:57.820
Ooh.

20:58.889 --> 21:00.823
- My life is r... My life is ruined.
- No.

21:00.891 --> 21:02.654
- It's... Yes, it's ruined.
- No. It's not.

21:02.726 --> 21:06.719
What about this?
Why don't you go back to the priesthood?

21:06.797 --> 21:10.198
I can't, okay?
L-I... I can't.

21:10.267 --> 21:13.964
You can't just go back, Dee.
"Yeah, I wanna become a priest again." You can't.

21:14.038 --> 21:17.166
- Okay?
- But are you sure? Did you double-check that?

21:17.241 --> 21:20.733
- Oh, my life is ruined.
- Hmm. So...

21:20.811 --> 21:23.974
I'm the bad person, huh?

21:29.219 --> 21:31.779
- That's what you get for not eating.
- Hey, Cricket!

21:31.855 --> 21:34.187
You know what would
make you feel better?

21:34.258 --> 21:37.819
- What could possibly make me feel better?
- You wanna tea-bag Dennis?

21:43.901 --> 21:45.835
- I'll get the camera!
- Yeah!

21:45.903 --> 21:47.700
- Polaroid, Polaroid, Polaroid.
- Whoo!
